# 📘 Assignment: Building REST APIs with FastAPI

## 🎯 Objective

Learn how to build a simple REST API using FastAPI. Students will define routes, validate request data, and return JSON responses while exploring the basics of modern API development.

## 📝 Tasks

### 🛠️ Set Up a FastAPI App

#### Description
Create a FastAPI application and add a root route that returns a welcome message.

#### Requirements
Completed program should:

- Install FastAPI and Uvicorn
- Create a FastAPI application instance
- Add a `GET /` endpoint that returns a JSON welcome message
- Run the app locally with Uvicorn

### 🛠️ Create and Read Items

#### Description
Build the basic HTTP endpoints needed to create and retrieve data from an in-memory list.

#### Requirements
Completed program should:

- Define an item model with an ID and required fields
- Add a `POST /items` route to create a new item
- Add a `GET /items` route to list all items
- Add a `GET /items/{item_id}` route to fetch a single item
- Return JSON data with meaningful status codes

### 🛠️ Update, Delete, and Validate

#### Description
Add the remaining CRUD operations and validate incoming request data with Pydantic models.

#### Requirements
Completed program should:

- Add a `PUT /items/{item_id}` route to update an item
- Add a `DELETE /items/{item_id}` route to remove an item
- Use request models to validate required fields and data types
- Return `404` when an item is not found
- Handle invalid input gracefully with clear error messages
